WEBVTT

00:08.070 --> 00:09.430
So cold!

00:13.430 --> 00:15.380
Sorry, Kagami,

00:15.990 --> 00:18.490
for forcing you to do the shoveling and all.

00:18.940 --> 00:20.510
Hey, no problem!

00:20.510 --> 00:22.870
Good luck with your studies today, Botan!

00:23.180 --> 00:24.820
Thanks!

00:26.950 --> 00:29.880
Wow, it really snowed a lot.

00:29.880 --> 00:31.380
Hyoma-san...

00:32.880 --> 00:35.540
Don't you need to cover up a little more?

00:37.390 --> 00:39.180
The worse the weather conditions,

00:39.180 --> 00:41.520
the better it is for psychological training.

00:42.000 --> 00:43.640
No, no, no...

00:43.640 --> 00:46.060
You're definitely gonna catch cold like that!

00:47.520 --> 00:47.650
<b>Hot Pack</b>

00:47.650 --> 00:47.770
<b>Hot Pack</b>

00:47.770 --> 00:48.650
<b>Hot Pack</b>

00:47.880 --> 00:48.650
Here.

00:49.020 --> 00:51.050
Humor me, okay?

00:56.410 --> 00:58.160
<b>Hot Pack</b>

00:56.700 --> 00:58.010
You have my gratitude.

00:58.010 --> 00:59.030
Farewell!

00:58.160 --> 00:58.280
<b>Hot Pack</b>

00:58.280 --> 00:58.410
<b>Hot Pack</b>

00:58.410 --> 00:58.530
<b>Hot Pack</b>

00:58.530 --> 00:59.030
<b>Hot Pack</b>

01:03.400 --> 01:06.030
He's like a mischievous little boy.

01:06.030 --> 01:09.290
Except he's all grown up.

01:10.610 --> 01:13.020
Well, I'm off.

01:13.020 --> 01:14.890
Have a nice day!

01:18.640 --> 01:20.110
Okay, then...

01:20.110 --> 01:21.310
Let's get back to it!

01:23.190 --> 01:24.260
Heya.

01:30.690 --> 01:33.190
Hey! It's been a while, hasn't it?

01:33.630 --> 01:36.200
I've got some questions for you, too,

01:36.560 --> 01:38.950
so I'm really happy you came...

01:39.400 --> 01:40.360
Aogi.

01:50.880 --> 01:58.630
<i>Malevolent Spirits</i>

03:11.960 --> 03:16.960
<b>Quickening</b>

03:24.070 --> 03:25.300
Here.

03:25.300 --> 03:27.210
Enjoy your tea!

03:31.770 --> 03:33.850
I'm an errand boy today.

03:33.850 --> 03:36.690
Once I've passed on my message, 
I'll be out of your hair.

03:37.130 --> 03:38.690
Now, now.

03:38.690 --> 03:44.490
Kagami's just mad because 
you hurt one of ours recently.

03:44.490 --> 03:45.700
One of yours?

03:46.220 --> 03:49.830
Our houseguest, Kunato Hyoma.

03:50.460 --> 03:53.050
You made contact in the course 
of your work, right?

03:53.050 --> 03:54.630
In the most predictable way.

03:56.580 --> 03:58.010
Make yourself comfortable.

04:00.000 --> 04:01.800
I have questions for you, too.

04:02.440 --> 04:07.300
I'd like to know how your employers 
reacted when you made your report.

04:08.370 --> 04:10.060
I bet you would.

04:10.460 --> 04:17.190
We bought your story about Kunato's reason 
for staying at the Nagatsuki household...

04:17.840 --> 04:23.200
But while we did pass it on, we have a 
handful of clients who have their doubts.

04:23.530 --> 04:28.490
You wanna know who might be 
pressing the issue pretty soon, right?

04:28.490 --> 04:29.870
Precisely.

04:30.300 --> 04:33.100
Can't give that up for free, though.

04:33.100 --> 04:36.250
You got any info of equal value for me?

04:36.650 --> 04:40.880
I have information that could be 
crucial to you in the very near future.

04:41.240 --> 04:42.280
Oh?

04:42.280 --> 04:46.590
You haven't been here in a while, 
so you may be unaware.

04:47.080 --> 04:50.600
Our neighborhood's grown 
quite dangerous of late.

04:51.720 --> 04:53.360
I'm not kidding.

04:53.360 --> 04:56.330
You could get jumped at any minute out there.

04:56.330 --> 04:59.380
It's dangerous for anyone 
walking around alone.

04:59.930 --> 05:00.980
But...

05:01.780 --> 05:04.490
I could recommend a route

05:04.490 --> 05:09.240
that would let you make it back safe, 
without any ill encounters.

05:09.240 --> 05:11.620
I-Is that a threat?!

05:11.620 --> 05:14.790
What? How could you suggest such a thing?

05:15.150 --> 05:19.820
Besides, you're the one who attacked 
the next head of House Kunato,

05:19.820 --> 05:21.750
who'd done nothing wrong.

05:22.410 --> 05:25.380
I think you owe us one for 
keeping that on the down low.

05:27.680 --> 05:30.970
I got over a dozen requests 
about the same thing,

05:30.970 --> 05:34.020
but most of 'em heard 
my report and backed down.

05:34.440 --> 05:38.270
"Kunato's staying with the Nagatsukis 
for training purposes."

05:38.270 --> 05:41.160
"That means the law hasn't been broken."

05:42.520 --> 05:44.780
Those folks will probably stay quiet.

05:45.370 --> 05:49.410
But I had three clients who remained... 
a little skeptical.

05:49.960 --> 05:53.630
The group of the tsukumogami 
you sealed that included Hikaki,

05:53.630 --> 05:56.220
known as the Sogenbi.

05:57.150 --> 06:01.260
The Saenome representative 
protecting Kyoto, the Kadomori Faction.

06:01.670 --> 06:06.300
And one of the Three Great Tsukumogami 
of Kyoto, the Bureau of Traditional Music.

06:06.670 --> 06:10.180
Those three didn't seem inclined 
to back off so easily.

06:10.920 --> 06:13.900
A human, like a tsukumogami, 
in whom a marebito dwells...

06:15.430 --> 06:18.520
Nagatsuki Botan possesses unknown potential.

06:19.280 --> 06:25.990
When there's a powerful human who could 
provoke it, like Kunato Hyoma, nearby...

06:27.260 --> 06:30.450
It's only a matter of time before 
someone offers up a complaint.

06:30.730 --> 06:34.840
The question is just if they come 
after you guys, the Kunato kid,

06:34.840 --> 06:38.720
Nagatsuki Botan herself, or all of you.

06:38.720 --> 06:40.830
But I wouldn't know.

06:41.280 --> 06:44.650
Might I ask which faction 
you think will move first?

06:45.290 --> 06:46.840
Let's see...

06:47.210 --> 06:49.470
Hang on! You can't make me share that, too!

06:49.470 --> 06:51.760
Oh, is that too much?

06:51.760 --> 06:54.100
Or maybe you can...

06:54.520 --> 06:58.070
Truth is, I've got a message 
from the lead-off hitter.

06:58.850 --> 07:02.730
Remember? I said I was 
playing errand boy today.

07:03.840 --> 07:05.470
They're calling you out.

07:05.470 --> 07:09.740
The group of the three with whom 
you've had the most dealings...

07:10.260 --> 07:12.820
Protectors of Kyoto, the Kadomori.

07:14.020 --> 07:17.110
The Saenome branch 
who watch over this region.

07:29.300 --> 07:30.220
Suzuri!

07:30.670 --> 07:31.970
Good work.

07:32.480 --> 07:33.880
You bet it was work!

07:33.880 --> 07:36.470
Why did I have to deal with him alone?

07:36.470 --> 07:39.610
Well, I'd... probably have hit him.

07:39.610 --> 07:42.730
And I can't keep my cool around Aogi.

07:42.730 --> 07:45.680
You're the only one he'd open up to.

07:45.680 --> 07:46.800
Yeah, yeah!

07:47.610 --> 07:50.140
That's our smooth talker!

07:50.140 --> 07:51.040
Good job!

07:51.040 --> 07:52.600
Oh, r-really?

07:52.600 --> 07:56.620
Well, I <i>did</i> think I'd handled it pretty well...

07:56.620 --> 08:01.390
But I was surprised to hear the Bureau 
of Traditional Music might get involved.

08:01.390 --> 08:03.560
Even Kai was happy to just wait and see...

08:04.440 --> 08:06.540
You think there are any others?

08:06.540 --> 08:08.190
Most likely.

08:08.190 --> 08:12.010
There are probably a few things 
Aogi's keeping close to his chest.

08:12.760 --> 08:13.930
Damn it!

08:13.930 --> 08:17.000
It's not like I was sworn 
to silence or anything,

08:17.000 --> 08:19.850
but it pisses me off that 
I had to tell him all that crap!

08:21.280 --> 08:24.120
I've got just one piece of info left.

08:24.120 --> 08:28.760
<i>No... that encounter the other 
day is still too ambiguous.</i>

08:32.280 --> 08:33.400
Hey.

08:33.780 --> 08:37.530
Were you the one investigating Kunato?

08:38.980 --> 08:40.290
<i>What?</i>

08:41.240 --> 08:43.560
<i>Is that... a tsukumogami?</i>

08:44.520 --> 08:48.010
Hey... tell me what you learned, would you?

08:48.790 --> 08:50.880
Can't give that up for free.

08:50.880 --> 08:53.670
You've gotta give me some info in exchange.

08:53.670 --> 08:55.320
For instance...

08:55.320 --> 08:58.050
Tell me who you are.

09:00.200 --> 09:01.560
Oh, really?

09:02.080 --> 09:03.430
Too bad.

09:09.410 --> 09:11.210
Creepy.

09:12.300 --> 09:16.320
<i>He's got the prestigious and the weirdos 
all coming out of the woodwork.</i>

09:16.320 --> 09:19.200
<i>Life's gonna be hard for that kid pretty soon.</i>

09:19.650 --> 09:21.610
Can't wait to see how it goes.

09:23.220 --> 09:27.340
Will he navigate the stormy 
seas coming his way?

09:28.670 --> 09:30.840
Hey, hey.

09:31.200 --> 09:33.710
Clothes really make the man, eh?

09:34.160 --> 09:38.640
I haven't yet received formal permission 
to act in Kyoto, after all.

09:38.640 --> 09:41.470
It's common sense to dress for the occasion.

09:41.470 --> 09:44.470
Even though they're my clothes?

09:44.810 --> 09:47.840
You ever met Kadomori before?

09:47.840 --> 09:48.590
No.

09:49.530 --> 09:52.540
But I heard about him from my grandfather.

09:53.940 --> 09:56.990
He puts up the front of a sly old man,

09:56.990 --> 09:58.470
but he's a bird of prey.

09:59.490 --> 10:02.950
Took you long enough to see me, 
but I won't hold it against you.

10:02.950 --> 10:05.680
Zohei told me the whole story.

10:05.680 --> 10:08.730
And I'm sure you've had your hands 
full getting acclimated here.

10:10.930 --> 10:12.440
<i>A bird of prey.</i>

10:12.840 --> 10:14.500
<i>An accurate description.</i>

10:14.960 --> 10:17.510
<i>The Saenome representative in Kyoto,</i>

10:17.950 --> 10:19.240
<i>Kadomori Taiju.</i>

10:25.840 --> 10:26.800
What is this?

10:26.800 --> 10:27.890
A call bell.

10:28.530 --> 10:33.270
The sounds he makes will call out 
any tsukumogami nearby.

10:33.270 --> 10:36.700
We made him a special exception 
since his power's so useful.

10:36.700 --> 10:39.420
He does good work for us.

10:39.420 --> 10:41.660
Why not sit down and watch with me?

10:46.510 --> 10:48.660
Regarding my license to act here...

10:49.160 --> 10:51.170
None of that, now.

10:51.600 --> 10:52.720
Who's that?

10:52.720 --> 10:55.170
Some Kunato kid.

10:55.170 --> 10:59.130
Hmph! Watching us work, eh? 
Must think he's hot shit.

10:59.130 --> 11:01.150
He's a spoiled brat from the sticks.

11:01.150 --> 11:04.430
Yeah, I know. Just stop talking.

11:04.930 --> 11:06.140
It's here.

11:10.570 --> 11:12.440
Time to get to work.

11:12.440 --> 11:14.890
There we go.

11:15.640 --> 11:17.190
Not gonna sit?

11:18.160 --> 11:19.750
Ah, youth.

11:29.190 --> 11:31.830
Our fights are more or less orthodox.

11:32.330 --> 11:35.840
We use the power of our talismans 
to hold down the target,

11:36.320 --> 11:40.840
and while they're frozen, 
drive sealing power into their dan tian.

11:37.840 --> 11:40.840
<b>Kadomori</b>

11:55.810 --> 11:57.230
<b>Kadomori</b>

11:57.960 --> 11:59.110
Seal.

12:09.040 --> 12:10.120
I see.

12:10.500 --> 12:14.600
<i>Kyoto is a battleground where 
tsukumogami spawn frequently.</i>

12:14.600 --> 12:17.380
<i>You'd need significant skill 
to keep it under control.</i>

12:18.320 --> 12:21.390
They're about average for us.

12:21.390 --> 12:24.130
As the next head of the Saenome, 
what do you think?

12:25.120 --> 12:26.390
Excellent.

12:26.390 --> 12:26.970
Tch.

12:28.210 --> 12:32.390
Nice to have the approval of 
a rich brat from nowheresville.

12:32.390 --> 12:34.390
He can hear you, dummy.

12:34.950 --> 12:38.900
Sorry, we've got our own share of issues.

12:39.200 --> 12:42.860
Too many hooligans in our ranks, for one thing.

12:42.860 --> 12:46.740
But worst of all, we're lacking in manpower.

12:47.650 --> 12:53.820
So I won't object if you want to keep 
up the business while you're here.

12:53.820 --> 12:56.040
I'd welcome it, in fact.

12:57.380 --> 12:59.850
I'm grateful to hear that.

13:00.930 --> 13:06.400
I know Zohei already gave his permission, 
but I figured I'd give it as well,

13:06.400 --> 13:08.180
as the local representative.

13:08.720 --> 13:11.070
Just report in every now and then.

13:11.070 --> 13:14.810
Also, could I ask you one more thing?

13:15.200 --> 13:16.300
Yes?

13:16.300 --> 13:17.370
Well...

13:18.350 --> 13:20.570
It's about the Nagatsuki household.

13:23.860 --> 13:28.200
The Heian Period was a time of great 
change in the history of Japanese poetry.

13:28.880 --> 13:32.490
<i>The Tale of Genji</i> integrated 
traditional poetry into prose,

13:32.010 --> 13:34.830
<i>Maybe I'll make stew tonight.</i>

13:32.490 --> 13:34.830
which had a massive influence 
on future generations...

13:35.990 --> 13:38.200
<i>Yeah, let's do stew.</i>

13:38.200 --> 13:39.420
<i>It'll warm us all up.</i>

13:40.780 --> 13:43.530
<i>I was really worried at first,</i>

13:43.530 --> 13:47.260
<i>but Hyoma-san's really feeling 
like a member of the family.</i>

13:48.550 --> 13:53.580
I'll admit, I was shocked 
when Aogi mentioned it to me.

13:54.570 --> 13:58.520
When I heard you were staying 
with the Nagatsukis,

13:58.520 --> 14:02.110
I thought the Kunato were 
finally making their move...

14:02.110 --> 14:06.860
But is it true you're really 
just there to observe?

14:07.200 --> 14:09.870
Yeah, that was a shock.

14:10.870 --> 14:12.620
Representative Kadomori.

14:12.620 --> 14:16.310
How does your clan view the Nagatsukis?

14:17.450 --> 14:22.480
Seems like monsters and 
monsters living side by side

14:22.480 --> 14:25.510
in one happy damn monster family.

14:27.370 --> 14:29.880
You've heard what Nagatsuki Botan is already?

14:30.380 --> 14:31.480
Yes.

14:31.480 --> 14:33.230
You get it, then.

14:33.230 --> 14:35.270
Outrageous, eh?

14:36.320 --> 14:42.090
What'll happen when that marebito 
inside her finally awakens?

14:42.450 --> 14:45.040
I've heard theories here and there,

14:45.040 --> 14:47.280
but I'd say the most likely one is...

14:47.820 --> 14:51.390
The same way a human 
takes ownership of objects,

14:51.390 --> 14:53.420
a human possessed by a marebito

14:53.420 --> 14:56.350
would have ownership of marebito.

14:56.350 --> 15:01.500
In other words, she'd become
the master of all tsukumogami...

15:01.500 --> 15:02.630
Or something like that.

15:04.440 --> 15:08.670
It'd be one thing if we could 
keep her under our control,

15:09.240 --> 15:13.910
but with no guarantee there, she's like 
a ticking time bomb in our midst.

15:14.620 --> 15:17.880
Who wouldn't want to get rid of it?

15:18.600 --> 15:23.690
The reason we can't is because she's 
got a wall around her at all times,

15:24.030 --> 15:26.880
and because her household 
isn't under our jurisdiction,

15:26.880 --> 15:30.450
but that of the leader of all Saenome.

15:30.780 --> 15:33.450
So there's no one else I can ask.

15:34.050 --> 15:39.720
You've made it inside the wall, 
and you're a Kunato on top of that.

15:40.990 --> 15:43.360
Would you seal up the Nagatsuki tsukumogami

15:43.360 --> 15:46.460
and do away with Nagatsuki Botan for us?

15:46.990 --> 15:49.520
I'd love to hear a yes.

15:49.520 --> 15:53.060
I might not be able to restrain my 
little band of hooligans otherwise.

15:53.470 --> 15:56.550
You get my meaning, don't you?

15:57.070 --> 15:57.970
My answer is no.

16:00.970 --> 16:01.940
My answer is no.

16:04.840 --> 16:08.020
I don't believe that 
Nagatsuki Botan is a monster.

16:08.610 --> 16:11.210
And as I consider myself 
a protector of humans,

16:11.210 --> 16:14.490
it would be unacceptable for 
me to "do away" with one.

16:14.490 --> 16:18.170
Furthermore, I have developed 
a fondness for that family.

16:19.640 --> 16:20.870
Therefore...

16:21.340 --> 16:22.340
My answer is no!

16:22.870 --> 16:25.380
H-He said it three times?

16:25.930 --> 16:27.720
Three times...

16:28.130 --> 16:30.130
<b>U
L
T
R
A
 
J
U
M
P</b>

16:33.890 --> 16:35.390
He means it, eh?

16:36.310 --> 16:38.390
Seems like he means it.

16:39.720 --> 16:43.640
And that means... what a fool I am.

16:47.720 --> 16:51.720
Of course a sheltered little boy 
would be hopelessly naïve.

16:52.140 --> 16:55.280
Politeness would've dictated 
an answer of "yes."

16:56.200 --> 16:58.920
I meant what I told you before.

16:59.340 --> 17:03.250
I couldn't dream of a better vessel for
 taking care of the Nagatsuki situation.

17:03.250 --> 17:06.440
I'll make use of you, 
even if I need to force you into it.

17:06.440 --> 17:09.500
Say "yes" now, and you can avoid a lot of pain.

17:10.000 --> 17:11.690
Well? Will you cooperate?

17:13.680 --> 17:14.760
No!

17:16.890 --> 17:19.840
Just as I'd expect of Zohei's grandson...

17:19.840 --> 17:20.890
A total fool.

17:23.820 --> 17:24.990
Go on, damn it!

17:24.990 --> 17:25.940
Oh, shut up!

17:35.810 --> 17:37.820
I have no intention of changing my mind.

17:39.540 --> 17:43.660
If you attempt to control me 
by force, I will fight back.

17:45.000 --> 17:47.250
How'd he endure that?!

17:47.720 --> 17:51.500
<i>Guess he's more than a little rich boy.</i>

17:51.820 --> 17:53.190
Saenome of Kyoto...

17:54.610 --> 17:55.590
Come to me.

17:58.970 --> 18:02.490
Guess he's got his share 
of battlefield experience.

18:04.420 --> 18:06.320
The fools got careless.

18:06.320 --> 18:10.310
Nice work, canceling out the 
explosive power of the talismans.

18:11.190 --> 18:15.420
Without protective charms or 
experience fighting tsukumogami,

18:15.420 --> 18:18.240
you wouldn't carry a talisman 
to cancel that out.

18:19.200 --> 18:20.330
Correct.

18:24.090 --> 18:27.840
But even if you've got real-life experience,

18:27.840 --> 18:31.390
the Tohoku region, 
overseen by the Kunato Clan,

18:31.390 --> 18:36.010
is a safe place full of meek 
and docile tsukumogami.

18:36.520 --> 18:41.510
About the only being there on par with 
the Three Great Tsukumogami of Kyoto...

18:44.180 --> 18:46.410
is the legendary monster that stole tiles

18:46.410 --> 18:49.420
from all houses that fell 
within the range of its power,

18:49.420 --> 18:54.000
and used them to destroy 
two villages in one night...

18:56.600 --> 18:59.530
The Onigawara of Ou.

19:01.800 --> 19:04.990
And they say the Onigawara 
went into seclusion, so...

19:04.990 --> 19:09.220
The place where you did the training 
that earned you so many scars...

19:10.230 --> 19:12.250
From our perspective,

19:12.870 --> 19:16.880
it's like a bonus stage without a boss.

19:17.640 --> 19:18.880
Those are...

19:19.270 --> 19:20.460
Control talismans?

19:21.230 --> 19:24.140
I see. You had them on the "call bell" earlier.

19:24.640 --> 19:27.300
Using talismans to control tsukumogami...

19:27.950 --> 19:29.900
That's how you do things, then?

19:30.390 --> 19:32.190
Exactly.

19:32.190 --> 19:36.270
Most of them are naughty brats 
we caught playing pranks.

19:36.270 --> 19:39.400
And our motto is to use 
whatever's available to us.

19:40.180 --> 19:44.520
Tsukumogami are just extensions 
of objects, anyway.

19:44.520 --> 19:46.910
We're just using those objects 
to the best of our ability.

19:47.360 --> 19:50.350
We'll make use of you later as well,

19:50.350 --> 19:54.170
so for now, enjoy a taste of a real battlefield.

19:58.940 --> 20:01.930
With pleasure.

20:03.190 --> 20:05.430
He's down for it?

20:05.430 --> 20:08.090
Matsu, you know what to do.

20:08.090 --> 20:12.690
Wear him down, then stick him 
with a binding talisman.

20:14.160 --> 20:15.690
Yeah, I know.

20:16.170 --> 20:19.350
Incidentally, I've been wondering...

20:19.840 --> 20:22.010
Who is that girl there?

20:23.950 --> 20:26.950
Oh, her?

20:27.520 --> 20:29.270
She's my daughter.

20:30.200 --> 20:33.120
Tsubaki, what's your pleasure?

20:33.500 --> 20:34.870
Going to take part?

20:39.640 --> 20:42.380
Nah, he's too cute. I'll pass.

20:42.380 --> 20:43.350
All right.

20:58.550 --> 20:59.770
<i>A tamasudare toy?</i>

21:18.800 --> 21:21.380
Is that... the Kunato Clan's...

21:22.310 --> 21:23.880
That shape...

21:24.630 --> 21:28.640
<i>The ritual tool of House Kunato, 
handed down directly from Saenokami...</i>

21:29.000 --> 21:31.040
<i>The "door pull," Chibiki-iwa.</i>

21:31.900 --> 21:34.890
<i>He's not hesitating to pull out all the stops.</i>

21:34.890 --> 21:38.030
<i>He'll do whatever it takes 
to kill tsukumogami.</i>

21:38.970 --> 21:42.650
<i>The kid's a little too ready for this.</i>

21:42.990 --> 21:46.900
<i>I'd heard his siblings were 
killed by a tsukumogami,</i>

21:47.480 --> 21:49.520
<i>but that hatred of his...</i>

21:49.520 --> 21:53.460
<i>He's nursed it far beyond what I expected.</i>

23:24.920 --> 23:39.930
<b>Next Time</b>

23:24.920 --> 23:39.930
<b>Circumstances</b>
